<title>USA: Chile to join Mercosur on Oct 1 -- Foreign Minister.</title>
<headline>Chile to join Mercosur on Oct 1 -- Foreign Minister.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile will join Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uraguay as an associate member of South America's free trade block, Mercosur, as of October 1, said Jose Insulza, Chile's Minister of Foreign Relations.</p>
<p>&quot;We in Chile are committed to open markets across South America as the best way to provide the opportunity of economic growth,&quot; Insulza told reporters here at a conference.</p>
<p>&quot;By joining Mercosur, we further demonstrate our countries committment to lower tariffs, greater trade, and continued growth through the region,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- J.P. Vicente, 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
